# Test: the daemon refuses to start on an IS-IS hostname outside 7-bit ASCII.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-fixit-config-validators-bypassed-at-startup AC-3 -- a
#            hand-edited hostname carrying an octet outside 0x20..0x7e is
#            refused at `ze` start, not only by `ze config validate`.
# PREVENTS:  the hole spec-fixit-isis-hostname-ascii depended on. That spec
#            makes the config boundary the ONLY enforcement point for RFC 5301
#            section 3: hostnameTLV is unchanged so the operator's octets reach
#            the wire byte for byte. With startup unvalidated, a hand-edited
#            hostname plus a restart still put 8-bit octets into TLV 137.
#
# test/isis/isis-hostname-ascii.ci proves `ze config validate` refuses the same
# value. This test proves the DAEMON refuses it, which is the claim that was
# false until LoadConfig gained its ValidateCustomSections call.
#
# RFC requirement: RFC5301-3-7 positive -- "The Value field is encoded in 7-bit ASCII" (RFC 5301 Section 3). The daemon refuses a UTF-8 name at load, so it can never be framed into TLV 137.
#
# The enforcing producer is ISISHostnameValidator
# (internal/component/config/validators.go), reached through the ze:validate
# extension on the hostname leaf in
# internal/plugins/isis/yang/ze-isis-conf.yang, walked by ValidateCustomSections
# (internal/component/config/validate_sections.go) from LoadConfig.

stdin=isis-utf8:terminator=EOF_UTF8
isis {
	net 49.0001.0000.0000.0001.00
	hostname café.example
}
EOF_UTF8

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=isis-utf8:exit=1:timeout=20s
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stderr:contains=config validation failed
expect=stderr:contains=isis
expect=stderr:contains=is not a valid IS-IS hostname
expect=stderr:contains=0xc3
expect=stderr:contains=7-bit ASCII
